One row per live association; the same counters as `quic`, per association,
plus send-credit state. Round-trip time and congestion window are not listed
because the transport does not expose them yet.eindexfmethodqquic_associationsdnamextelemetry.quic_associationsgrequest°ffieldsÄhresponse°ffieldsÅ§kdescriptionxOne row per live association.dnamelassociationsctagdtypeqQuicAssociation[]gsummaryx5Return QUIC transport state for each live associationdtierhinternaljvisibilityfpublic™icomponentitelemetrycdocyTarget platforms: A L E. E reports a row for `now` and `udp6` (the bearers that keep
these counters); A and L report a row for every bearer registered on the node,
from the node's own per-bearer counters. Fields a bearer does not count are omitted
(`rx_rejected` is not kept by the node).

One row per bearer the node runs. These are the bearer's own submission and
receive facts; QUIC's view of the same traffic is in `quic`. Bearer-specific
detail stays in that bearer's method (`ble.status`, `now`, `nan`, `udp6`).eindex	fmethodgbearersdnameqtelemetry.bearersgrequest°ffieldsÄhresponse°ffieldsÅ§kdescriptionsOne row per bearer.dnamegbearersctagdtypepBearerCounters[]gsummaryx&Return common counters for each bearerdtierhinternaljvisibilityfpublic™icomponentitelemetrycdocy-Target platforms: A L E, with fields omitted where the platform has no such
